{
  "about": "Cross-language contract. Every binding traces each case. `form` is `encoded` (the file's bytes go to trace) or `rgba` (the file is raw straight RGBA8 of `width` x `height`, for trace_rgba). `expect` must match on every build: the reported width and height, or `error`, the kind of error (invalid_image, invalid_options, internal). `svg` maps a build target (the library's build_target()) to the SVG's length in bytes and SHA-256; a target with an entry must match it exactly, a target without one is checked on everything else. `same_svg_as` names a case whose SVG must be identical, on every target. Cases, inputs and options are written by hand; `expect` and `svg` are produced by the Rust facade.",
  "regenerate": "INKVEC_BLESS=1 cargo test -p inkvec --release --test contract (output changed: rewrites this target, drops the others); INKVEC_BLESS=add ... (records another target's hashes)",
